          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did āśīrvādaḥ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अग्निः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अग्निः (agniḥ) — \"fire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अग्निः (agniḥ) is fire itself — the flame on a hearth, and the fire an offering is poured into."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have had the doing-word for a while: दहति, \"burns\". अग्निः (agniḥ) is the thing that does it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin ignis is the very same word, and English carries it in ignite and igneous; Russian ogon' is another of its brothers. It went west almost unchanged, and in Sanskrit it stands as the first word of the oldest hymn there is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fire, named as a thing rather than as an action."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
