          "title": "You'll want to know: भस्म",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भस्म (bhasma) — \"ash\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भस्म (bhasma) is what अग्निः (agniḥ) leaves behind — ash, and the grey line of it drawn across a forehead."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It stands on bhas, \"to chew, to grind small\", so ash is the ground-down thing: what is left when fire has finished eating."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hindi and Marathi keep bhasm with the meaning untouched."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fire, and what fire leaves."
            }
          ]
        },
