          "title": "You'll want to know: शिला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिला (śilā) — \"a stone, a slab of rock\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शिला (śilā) is a stone large enough to sit on: a slab, a flat rock, the piece a step is cut from."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Beside पर्वतः, which is the whole raised land, शिला (śilā) is one piece of it you can put a hand on."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its history outside India is unsettled — nobody has agreed a cousin for it, the way nobody has for केशः or माला. Feminine, ending in -आ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One piece of the mountain, small enough to touch."
            }
          ]
        },
